      "extract": "The Neumann–Zagier matrices of an ideal triangulation are integer matrices with symplectic properties whose entries encode the number of tetrahedra that wind around each edge of the triangulation. They can be used as input data for the construction of a number of quantum invariants that include the loop invariants, the 3D-index and state-integrals. We deﬁne a twisted version of Neumann–Zagier matrices, describe",
